**Final Result:** 100% — All 10 tasks completed successfully

## 1. Project Overview

This capstone project involved using Terraform to provision and configure AWS infrastructure as code. The objective was to practise foundational cloud infrastructure management by creating resources, configuring access policies, managing storage and secrets, and establishing virtual networking.

Each task was completed in the prescribed Terraform working directory and used a `main.tf` configuration where required. The project reinforced the infrastructure-as-code workflow: initialize the provider, format and validate configurations, review the execution plan, apply changes, and inspect Terraform state to verify the resulting resources.

